2. Status has color  
3. Grid is occupying full screen

Pont 1 & 2 will be achieved in the upcoming sessions. For point 3 we can achieve this by setting screentype of pa\_complaints as **fit\_to\_area** and mark **auto\_height** as true for s\_complaints layout.


| 📸  Tree View — How s\_complaints Looks in the Page Builder Tree After building s\_complaints, it should appear in the tree as shown below — with ticket\_id as a navigation link, all property controls, conf\_grid000, and section\_toolbar. |
| :---- |

![][image8]

*Page Builder tree showing s\_complaints with controls: ticket\_id (link icon), customer\_id, priority, s\_status, planned\_res\_dat, closed\_on, sales\_manager, plus conf\_grid000 config and section\_toolbar*

### **B.10 — Step 5: Create the Detail Page Area (pa\_complaint\_details)**

The detail area loads when a complaint row is selected from the list. It contains a toolbar for actions, a header section showing critical fields, and a tabbed area for all complaint details.

| 1 | Right-click pl\_complaints\_desk → New → Page Area. Rename: pa\_complaint\_details. |
| :---: | :---- |
| **2** | Update screentype as tab |

### **B.10.2 — Creating the Detail Header Section (s\_detail\_header)**

The header section displays the most critical complaint fields prominently. screenType: card. Bound to d\_complaints\_detail TransNode.

| 1 | Right-click pa\_complaint\_details → New → Section. Rename: s\_detail\_header. |
| :---: | :---- |
| **2** | Set screenType \= card. Set TransNode path \= detail. |
| **3** | Add controls from d\_complaints\_detail unused properties: desc, s\_status, priority, res\_team, responsible\_tea. ⇒ change the control to m.Text for making it readable only |
| **4** | Save. |

| 📸  Final Output — After Creating s\_detail\_header Once s\_detail\_header is created with all controls and you click Show Full Preview, you will see the result as mentioned below after modeling which will be covered in upcoming sessions |
| :---- |

![][image9]

| 📸  Tree View — How s\_detail\_header Looks in the Page Builder Tree After creating s\_detail\_header with all header controls, it should appear as shown below. |
| :---- |

![][image10]

*Page Builder tree showing s\_detail\_header with controls: desc, i\_ageing (icon), t\_ageing (text), s\_status, i\_t\_priority (priority icon), i\_res\_team (team icon), responsible\_tea*

### **B.10.3 — Creating the Detail Area (pa\_comp\_details)**

pa\_comp\_details is a nested Page Area inside pa\_complaint\_details.

| 1 | Right-click page area→ New → Page Area. Rename: pa\_comp\_details. |
| :---: | :---- |
| **2** | In the Detail panel, set screenType \= default. Set showTitle \= true  & title \= detail so tab labels are visible. |
| **3** | Assign the page area to pa\_complaints\_detail. |
| **4** | Now create all 4 sections inside pa\_comp\_details. Right-click pa\_comp\_details → New → Section for each. Set each to screenType \= form Set TransNode \= detail for form sections. |
| **5** | Set each section’s title property — this becomes the tab label visible at runtime. |
| **5** | Assign all 4 sections to pa\_comp\_details in the correct sequence. Save. |
| **6** | Set type \= header for s\_detail\_header layout & type \= section for pa\_comp\_details. |
| **7** | Set press event for complaint\_id link with function as navTo \=\> pageArea : pa\_complaint\_details. |

| Section ID | Screen Type | Tab Title / Contents |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| **s\_complaint\_details** | form | Complaint Details — complaint\_id, complaint\_type, description, priority, status, customer\_id |
| **s\_assigment\_details** | form  | Assignment — responsible\_team, manager, first response date, planned resolution date |
| **s\_timeline\_details** | form  | TAT & Timeline — actual\_tat, standard\_tat, closed\_on, created\_on, modified\_on |
| **s\_admin\_info** | form  | Contains s\_created\_by, s\_modified\_by, s\_created\_on and s\_modified\_on |

### **B.10.3 — Add Action buttons for pa\_comp\_details** {#b.10.3-—-add-action-buttons-for-pa_comp_details}

| 1 | Right-click pa\_comp\_details→ New → Toolbar. |
| :---: | :---- |
| **2** | Set showAdd and ShowDelete \= false  |
| **3** | Right-click section-Toolbar → New → Action/Button. |
| **4** | Right-click button01 → rename → edit  |
| **5** | Set text \= Edit | icon \= sap-icon://edit | add press event  and  fill this.setMode('EDIT') |
| **6** | Repeat steps 3,4 and 5 for **save** with this.saveTransaction("Data saved successfully.", "Save Failed.", true, true) |
| **7** | Repeat steps 3,4 and 5 for **cancel** with this.refreshTransnode("complaints\_detail","DISPLAY",true) |

| 📸  Final Output — After Creating pa\_comp\_details |
| :---- |

![][image11]

| 📸  Tree View — How pa\_complaint\_details Looks After Full Setup |
| :---- |

![][image12]

*Page Builder tree showing pa\_complaint\_details with: section\_toolbar, s\_detail\_header, and nested pa\_comp\_details containing all 7 tab sections — s\_complaint\_details, s\_complaint\_details3, s\_complaint\_details5, s\_reporter\_details, s\_complaint\_details2, s\_complaint\_details4, s\_complaint\_item*

### **B.11 — Step 6: Preview and Verify the Complete Screen**

| 1 | Save all changes in the Page Builder. |
| :---: | :---- |
| **2** | Click Show Full Preview. The screen loads with live complaint data from the database. |
| **3** | Verify the search bar appears at the top: Ticket Id, Status, Complaint Type, Escalated, Employee Category, Priority fields visible. Close / Reset / Search buttons present. |
| **4** | Verify the complaint list appears below the search bar with columns: ticket\_id (clickable link), customer\_id, priority, status, planned resolution date, closed date. |
| **5** | Click a complaint row. Verify the detail area loads with the header section (description, status, priority) and the tab area below. |
| **6** | Navigate through each tab — Complaint Details, Assignment, Reporter Info, TAT & Timeline, Complaint Items. Verify correct fields in each. |
| **7** | If a section appears blank: select it in the tree and check that its TransNode path is correctly set in the Detail panel. Ensure Fold From is set on d\_complaints\_detail. |

| ✔  UI Build Checkpoint — Verify Before Session 3 p\_complaints page created with pl\_complaints\_desk as default layout. Page Data Model has d\_complaints\_list (EntitySet) and d\_complaints\_detail (Entity, Fold From: list). pa\_complaints: s\_search (search, all filter fields) \+ s\_complaints (grid, 7 columns incl. navigation link). pa\_complaint\_details: section\_toolbar \+ s\_detail\_header (form, header fields) \+ pa\_comp\_details (tab). pa\_comp\_details: 7 tab sections including s\_complaint\_item (grid) for complaint line items. Full Preview shows the search bar — exact match with the reference screenshots from the trainer. Clicking a complaint row loads the detail area with all tabs populated. |
| :---- |

## Session 2 — BOL — Entity Fundamentals & Initial Pages {#session-2}
 Assignment {#session-2-assignment}

Complete all mandatory tasks before Session 3\. The trainer will verify each item at the start of Session 3\.

* Create all 5 remaining entities with correct properties and schema updated for each.

* Insert 3 test records in d\_customers and d\_resp\_team via Data Browser.

* Build p\_complaints\_manual manually (Parts B.2 – B.8). Full Preview must show complaint cards and detail form loading on card selection.

* Compare p\_complaints (wizard) with p\_complaints\_manual (manual) in preview — both must render the same data.

* Document any questions or issues encountered — bring to Session 3 Q\&A.

| Session 3 — Entity Configuration Duration: Full day  |  Pre-requisite: Session 2 assignment verified |
| :---- |

## Session 3 — Entity Configuration (Relations, Object Types, Status, ID Series) {#session-3}


By the end of this session, you will be able to:

* Understand what Entity Relations are and create Primary and Non-Primary (Aggregated) relations between entities.

* Understand what Object Types are, why they are needed, and configure complaint type classifications for d\_complaints.

* Configure Status and Status Groups to represent the complaint lifecycle (OPEN → INPROCESS → ON HOLD → RESOLVED → CLOSED → REOPEN).

* Set up an ID Series for complaint\_id to auto-generate readable complaint numbers (e.g. CMP-00001).

* Update the p\_complaints UI to reflect the new entity configuration — making the complaint\_type, status, and complaint\_id fields work correctly in the page.

| 📘  What This Session Builds On |
| :---- |
| Session 1 created the application, roles, users, and d\_complaints entity with raw properties. |
| Session 2 created the remaining 5 entities and built the full p\_complaints page step by step. |
| Session 3 enriches the d\_complaints entity with the platform features that turn raw fields into intelligent, lifecycle-aware data. |
| After Session 3, the complaint\_id will auto-generate, the status dropdown will show the correct lifecycle values, and complaint\_type will be classified. |
|  |

