## Part C — Creating VH Query Value Helps

## **C.1 — What Is VH Query?**

A VH Query fetches its suggestion items from a live entity or modelled query at runtime. Unlike VH Config (which is static metadata), VH Query shows records that are currently in the transactional database. This is the right choice for master entity pickers — where the data comes from d\_customers, d\_resp\_team, or any other entity that can be searched and selected.

| 📘  VH Query Fields (BOL Editor 7.0 User Guide — Section 2.2.3 Value Help Detail) |
| :---- |
| Entity/Query: The entity name or modelled query ID that returns the list of suggestions. |
| Key Property: The property whose value gets STORED in the parent entity when the user selects an item. For d\_customers → customer\_id. |
| Display Text: The property shown to the user in the dropdown/picker. For d\_customers → customer\_name. |
| Desc Format: How the display appears. Example: :customer\_id--:customer\_name shows ID followed by Name. |
| Icon: Optional — entity property that holds an icon URL to show alongside each suggestion item. |
|  |

## **C.2 — Step-by-Step: Creating vhq\_customer**

| \# | Action | Detail |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| **1** | **Click \+ → Value Help** | Select entity and In the Data Studio toolbar, click \+ → Value Help. Value Help ID: vhq\_customer | Value Help Type: QUERY. Click Create. |
| **2** | **Open vhq\_customer** | Click vhq\_customer in the tree. The Detail panel shows the VH Query configuration fields. |
| **3** | **Set Entity/Query** | In the Entity/Query field, select d\_customers. This means the VH will execute a runtime query against d\_customers to fetch suggestion rows. |
| **4** | **Set Key Property** | Key Property: customer\_id. This is the value that gets written into d\_complaints.customer\_id when the user picks a customer. |
| **5** | **Set Display Text** | Display Text: customer\_name. This is what the user sees in the dropdown list. |
| **6** | **Set Desc Format** | Desc Format: :customer\_id--:customer\_name. This renders as 'CUST-001 \-- Acme Corp' in the picker field once a value is selected. |
| **7** | **Save** | Click Save. vhq\_customer is ready. |

     Perform the same for vhq\_res\_team

## **C.4 — Assign VH Query to Entity Properties**

| \# | Action | Detail |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| **1** | **Select d\_complaints → Properties tab** | Click on d\_complaints in the tree and go to Properties. |
| **2** | **Assign vhq\_customer to customer\_id** | Click the Value Help cell for customer\_id. Select vhq\_customer from the picker. Optionally mark Is Restricted \= true to enforce that only valid customer records can be entered. |
| **3** | **Assign vhq\_resp\_team to responsible\_team** | Click the Value Help cell for responsible\_team. Select vhq\_resp\_team. |
| **4** | **Save** | Click Save. |

| 💡  VH Type in the UI Control (KloControls 7.0 User Guide — KloInput) |
| :---- |
| After assigning a VH to a property, the KloInput control in the UI renders differently based on the vhType setting in the Page Data Model or the control's properties panel. |
| F4: Shows a full picker dialog when the user clicks the input — best for large datasets (d\_customers with many records). |
| ComboBox: Shows a dropdown list — best for small fixed lists (priority, complaint\_type). |
| AutoComplete: Shows suggestions as the user types — best for name-search scenarios. |
| The platform automatically uses the appropriate type based on the VH type. You can override it in the Page Data Model or the control properties. |
|  |

## Part D — Understanding and Creating KloQueries

## **D.1 — What Is a KloQuery?**

A KloQuery is the Klobase equivalent of a SQL SELECT statement. It lets you define — within the Data Studio — exactly what records to fetch, from which entity, with which filters, joins, and sort order. Unlike a Runtime Entity Query (which simply fetches all records of an entity), a Modelled Query gives you full control over the WHERE clause, JOIN entities, and sort order — and is reusable across multiple pages.

| Query Type | When to Use |
| :---- | :---- |
| Runtime Query (Entity Query) | Fetch all records of a single entity. No WHERE clause in the definition. Filters applied at runtime via the TransNode. Use for simple list screens. |
| Modelled Query (Dynamic Query) | Define custom WHERE conditions, joins, sort order in the BOL Editor. Reusable, entity-independent. Use for role-filtered lists (My Complaints), VH Queries backed by joins, aggregated results. |
| Native Query (Advanced Query) | Raw SQL. Database-specific. Use only for special cases not achievable with modelled queries. Avoid training. |

| 📘  KloQuery Fields Reference (BOL Editor 7.0 User Guide — Section 3.0.2) |
| :---- |
| Return Entity: The entity whose properties appear in the result set. |
| Query Type: Runtime | Modelled | Native — affects which tabs are available. |
| Entities And Join: Add the root entity and any joined entities (LEFT JOIN, INNER JOIN, etc.). |
| Select Properties: Choose which properties from the entities appear in the result. |
| Parameters: Define input parameters the query accepts at runtime (e.g., user\_id filter passed from the TransNode). |
| Where: Define filter conditions: entity.property \= :parameter or entity.property \= 'fixed\_value'. |
| Sort Order: Set the default sorting column and direction (ASC / DESC). |
| Naming convention: Query IDs must start with q\_. All lowercase. |
|  |

